{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1476862480,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxODM4ODY4OTk=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1032","origin":"github"},"title":"SSH ControlPath in inappropriate location","message":"```\nIn [5]: ssh = sm.get_connection('localhost:/tmp/dummy')\nIn [6]: ssh.open()\nmih@localhost's password: \nIn [7]: ssh.open()\nIn [8]: ssh.ctrl_path\nOut[8]: '/home/mih/.config/datalad/localhost'\n```\n\nssh_config(5) says:\n\n\u003e It is recommended that any ControlPath used for opportunistic connection sharing include at least %h, %p, and %r (or alternatively %C) and be placed in a directory that is not writable by other users.\n\nThis is not true in our default setup.\n\nThe placement of the socket might also be related to the issues of SSH connections not being reused #826 #865 (of which at least the former is still present in master as of now). Moreover, the control master socket is no config file. I could imagine people having their `.config` in a VCS.\n\nThe socket could go into `~/cache/datalad/sockets` which would be made `700`. Actual target directory should come from a config setting.\n\nOne more: We do `ControlPersist=yes`. Are we 100% positive that under any circumstances we will not leave behind something that could be used for (un)intentional evil? Or should we at least use something like `ControlPersist=1h`?\n\n@bpoldrack?","files":null}]}